{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" generates that class for you (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<StructName>Observer"},{"text":") and wires up the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe"},{"text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","type":"heading","text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers take ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". They never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":", never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"throw"},{"type":"text","text":", and never call I\/O directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","type":"heading","text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" runs effects in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","type":"heading","text":"4. Persistence is invisible"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" properties; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" records every change in a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You never write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","type":"heading","text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","type":"heading","text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two structural patterns:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" for undo; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" keypaths for persistence).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does this need to know your action type?","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","type":"heading","text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Form inputs use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding(get:set:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to read from the store and dispatch on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":". Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and write back on a button."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", those plugins are blind to it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","type":"heading","text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The recommended order:"}]},{"code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","type":"heading","text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"type":"text","text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@concurrent"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async\/await"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","type":"heading","text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux gives you a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppEnvironment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A network layer (use ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and Swidux doesn’t care).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Anti-patterns","type":"heading","text":"Anti-patterns"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"try","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from inside a reducer — use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Owning the store with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — use ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"ObservableObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Buffering form state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Registering ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" before ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" — snapshot must precede mutation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Design Principles","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"generated":true,"title":"Explanation","anchor":"Explanation"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"title":"StateWriter","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"title":"Send","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"topic","title":"ChangeSet","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","type":"topic","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"title":"PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"topic","title":"Plugin Architecture","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"title":"Build Your First Swidux App","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"title":"Architecture & Performance","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"title":"UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"title":"Effect","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","title":"EntityStore","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}]}}}